.TH MAN 7
.SH NAME
man \- how a manual page is written
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&.\e" Part of SIEOS. (c) Olivier Moulin. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
\&.\e" source: user/NAME/NAME.c
\&.TH NAME SECTION
\&.SH NAME
name[, other] \e\- what it does, in one line
\&.SH SYNOPSIS
\&...
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The pages are kept in
.BI man/ section / name . section
of SIEOS's sources, in a small part of the classic
.B man
macros: a line that starts with a dot is a macro, any other line is text,
filled into lines as wide as the screen. The same file is read by
.BR man (1)
on SIEOS, by
.B tools/man.py
on the build machine (the web pages and the checks), and by groff
.RB ( "groff \-man \-Tutf8" ).
.SS Macros
.TP
.BI .TH " name section"
the page's title (first)
.TP
.BI .SH " heading"
a section: NAME, SYNOPSIS, DESCRIPTION, OPTIONS, EXIT STATUS, FILES,
EXAMPLES, SEE ALSO, BUGS, in that order (and what a page needs: COMMANDS,
MESSAGES, RETURN VALUE, ERRORS)
.TP
.BI .SS " heading"
a part of a section
.TP
.BR .PP ", " .LP ", " .P
a new paragraph
.TP
.B .TP
a tagged paragraph: the next line is the tag (an option), the text after
it is indented
.TP
.BI .IP " tag"
the same, its tag on the macro's line
.TP
.BR .RS ", " .RE
indent further, and back
.TP
.BR .nf ", " .fi
lines as they are (examples, code), and filled again
.TP
.BR .br ", " .sp
a new line, an empty line
.TP
.BI .B " words" "\fR, \fP" .I " words"
in bold (what is typed as it is), underlined (what stands for something);
alone, the next line
.TP
.BR .BR ", " .RB ", " .BI ", " .IB ", " .IR ", " .RI
words alternately in the two fonts, without spaces between them:
.B ".BR sh (1),"
.TP
.B .\e"
a comment; the first lines tell the license and, after
.BR source: ,
the files whose code reads the options the page shows
.SS Escapes
.B \efB
bold,
.B \efI
underlined,
.B \efR
plain,
.B \efP
the font before;
.B \e\-
a minus sign (options are written
.BR \e\-l );
.B \ee
a backslash;
.B \e&
nothing (before a dot that starts a line of text);
.BR \e(bu ,
.BR \e(em ,
.BR \e(mu ,
.BR \e(lq ,
.B \e(rq
a bullet, a dash, a times sign, quotes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B man/
the pages, in SIEOS's sources
.TP
.B /usr/share/man/
the pages on the disk, without their comment lines, and
.B whatis
.TP
.B build/man-html/
.B make man-html
puts the web pages there, with an index
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (1),
.BR intro (7)
.PP
.B make man-check
(part of
.BR "make test" )
fails unless every program in /bin and every system call has a page, every
option a page of section 1 or 8 shows is found in its program's source,
and every page SEE ALSO names exists.
